      <h2 id="related">Where to go next</h2>
      <p>If the racket is not your limiting factor, the next thing worth an evening's attention is where you are standing when the shuttle arrives: <a href="/guides/badminton-doubles-positioning">badminton doubles positioning</a> covers the two shapes and when to switch between them, and costs nothing.</p>
      <p>If you are kitting out a club rather than yourself, <a href="/guides/how-to-start-a-badminton-club">how to start a badminton club</a> deals with nets, posts, shuttles and what a hall actually needs.</p>

      <div style="margin-top:34px;padding-top:22px;border-top:1px solid var(--line)">
        <h4 style="margin:0 0 8px">How this guide was put together</h4>
        <p style="color:var(--muted-2);font-size:.95rem;margin:0">ePegboard builds club-night software. We are not coaches, we do not sell rackets, and we have not tested one. The performance claims here come from published research, the legal ones from the Laws of Badminton, and the market ones from our own survey.</p>
        <p style="color:var(--muted-2);font-size:.95rem;margin:12px 0 0"><strong>The survey:</strong> on 23 August 2026 we read the public product feeds of two UK specialist badminton retailers, giving 234 adult rackets after excluding junior rackets and multi-racket sets. Prices are the lowest listed variant on the day, sale prices included. Specifications are the retailers' own product tags, which describe how a racket is <em>marketed</em> rather than measurements we took. It is a one-day snapshot of two catalogues and we did not weigh, string or hit anything.</p>
        <p style="color:var(--muted-2);font-size:.95rem;margin:12px 0 0"><strong>Sources:</strong> <a href="https://system.bwfbadminton.com/documents/folder_1_81/Statutes/CHAPTER-4---RULES-OF-THE-GAME/SECTION%204.1-%20Laws%20of%20Badminton.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">BWF Laws of Badminton, Law 4</a> &middot; <a href="https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-023-37108-x" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Towler, Mitchell &amp; King (2023) on swingweight and shuttle speed</a> &middot; <a href="https://doi.org/10.1080/02640414.2020.1792132" target="_blank" rel="noopener">McErlain-Naylor et al. (2020) on impact location</a> &middot; <a href="https://revistaseug.ugr.es/index.php/IJRSS/article/view/33203" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Phomsoupha, Ibrahime &amp; Laffaye on shaft deflection</a> &middot; <a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/38761131/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Musculoskeletal injuries in badminton (2024 review)</a> &middot; <a href="https://www.victor-europe.com/blog/article/how-to-pick-the-right-badminton-rackets-for-beginners" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Victor on choosing a beginner racket</a></p>
        <p style="color:var(--muted-2);font-size:.9rem;margin:12px 0 0">Published 23 August 2026 by ePegboard.</p>
      </div>

